  "summary": "A run of preprints pushes qLDPC and surface-code decoding toward sub-microsecond latency while matching or beating BP+OSD, Relay-BP and Tesseract accuracy.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is decoding under real-time constraints, increasingly for qLDPC codes rather than only surface codes. SCOPE reports a logical error rate of 4.82e-10 on the [[144,12,12]] bivariate bicycle code with 173.8 ns latency. TEMPO-BP adapts per-variable memory via local feedback and outperforms BP+OSD and Relay-BP. Pêlagos scales Relay-BP across multiple GPUs. TCBP-JOBS learns calibrated fault probabilities and matches Tesseract accuracy. For surface codes, Beyond Blossom accelerates CPU MWPM with local predecoding, and a survey frames these efforts as decoder- and code-level hierarchies. Adjacent work co-designs codes and circuits: Armillary qLDPC codes exceed rate 1/2 on fixed-connectivity superconducting hardware, Proxima schedules syndrome extraction using a DEM-based metric, and trapped-ion sliding-window decoding uses soft outputs. Hardware results cover temporally correlated leakage in 7x7 surface-code stability experiments and magic state cultivation on IBM devices.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
